 ## Overview
-This method generates text embeddings for 3D Gaussian Splatting by encoding language prompts into latent vectors using a frozen CLIP text encoder [S1, unofficial]. It distinguishes itself from standard text embedding by appending directional view descriptors (e.g., "front", "side") to the prompt, allowing the system to associate specific semantic concepts with specific camera viewpoints [S1, unofficial][S2]. This enables directional-dependent rendering and open-vocabulary queries that respect spatial orientation [S1, unofficial][S2].
+This method generates text embeddings for 3D Gaussian Splatting by encoding language prompts into latent vectors using a frozen CLIP text encoder [S1, unofficial]. It distinguishes itself from standard text embedding by appending directional view descriptors (e.g., "front", "side") to the prompt, allowing the system to associate specific semantic concepts with specific camera viewpoints [S1, unofficial][S2]. This enables directional-dependent rendering and open-vocabulary queries that respect spatial orientation, contrasting with sibling methods like [3D Gaussian Splatting with Feature Vectors](8060-3d-gaussian-splatting-with-feature-vectors.md) and [LSeg Feature Encoding](12078-lseg-feature-encoding.md) that focus on spatial feature maps rather than language-conditioned directional prompts [S1, unofficial][S2].
 
